The user wants us to create files `index.html` and `meta.json` initially (Task 1). The previous attempts failed because the assistant never wrote those files. The user now asks to fix the errors, which are basically that the file does not exist. We need to create the `index.html` and `meta.json` files.

Thus we must write them using the write tool.

We have to use the reference example's structure as a template but not copy the game code (the asteroids), and we need to produce a minimal scaffold that loads without console errors.

Given the constraints: the file should have HTML skeleton with header, canvas, restart button, and empty script block. meta.json containing header content.

Thus we need to create index.html with proper HTML and a `<script>` tag that contains the skeleton sections as placeholders that follow the reference structure (i.e., the comment section dividers etc). However we could make minimal valid HTML content that contains an empty script, but the reference example includes many sections. However we were required: "Use the reference example above as a structural template — section divider banners, `keys` Set input pattern, etc." But for now, Task 1 only includes HTML scaffold and meta.json. So we need to produce the top-level skeleton which includes at least the `SCRIPT` tag with placeholder sections. However the user said: "HTML scaffold + meta.json — create required HTML skeleton with header, canvas, restart button, and empty script block; generate meta.json matching the header content."

Thus we only need HTML skeleton: header with title, description, controls (list). Canvas element with id 'game' and a button with id 'restart', and a script block (empty). So the script block is empty, not needing any sections yet. Our earlier attempts didn't create any files.

Thus we must create index.html and meta.json. Write them using the write tool.

We need to determine the correct content for meta.json and index.html.

The title: "Orbit Swirl". The description: extract from design perhaps. The title given in prompt. The meta.json structure matches the reference: keys: title, description, controls, tags.

We need to include controls. Based on design, the controls are tapping to reverse direction. Let's list typical controls: "Tap/click to reverse direction", maybe "Press R or click Restart". Since it's a simple stub, we can use placeholder.

Also tags: maybe ["arcade", "reflex", "orbit"].

Thus we need to create meta.json like:

{
  "title": "Orbit Swirl",
  "description": "Orbiting dot reverses direction on tap, dodging obstacles in radial lanes.",
  "controls": [
    "Tap / click to reverse orbit direction",
    "Press R or click Restart"
  ],
  "tags": ["arcade", "reflex", "orbit"]
}

Now HTML: Provide <header class="game-header"> etc as example. Use similar style as reference, but not required. Probably best to just reuse the header from reference but adjust content.

Thus index.html:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>Orbit Swirl</title>
  <style>
    body {margin:0;background:#0a0a0f;color:#e6e6f0;font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}
    .game-header {padding:12px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid #1d1d2a;}
    .game-header h1 {margin:0;font-size:18px;color:#7df9ff;}
    .game-header .game-description {margin:4px 0;color:#a5a5b8;}
    .game-header .game-controls {margin:4px 0;padding-left:18px;color:#c8c8d8;}
    main {display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;padding:16px;}
    canvas {background:#05050c;border:1px solid #2a2f44;}
    .game-restart {margin-top:10px;padding:8px 14px;background:#1c2030;color:#7df9ff;border:1px solid #2a2f44;cursor:pointer;}
    .game-restart:hover {background:#232842;}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="game-header">
    <h1>Orbit Swirl</h1>
    <p class="game-description">Orbiting dot reverses direction on tap, dodging obstacles in radial lanes.</p>
    <ul class="game-controls">
      <li>Tap / click to reverse orbit direction</li>
      <li>Press R or click Restart</li>
    </ul>
  </header>
  <main>
    <canvas id="game" width="800" height="600"></canvas>
    <button id="restart" class="game-restart" type="button">Restart</button>
  </main>
  <script>
    // === CONFIG =============================================================
    // Placeholder for future configuration
    // === STATE ==============================================================
    // Placeholder for game state objects
    // === RESET ==============================================================
    // Placeholder for reset logic
    // === LOOP/UPDATE ========================================================
    // Placeholder for animation loop
    // === RENDER ============================================================
    // Placeholder for render logic
    // === INPUT ==============================================================
    // Placeholder for input handling
    // === AUDIO ==============================================================
    // Placeholder for audio handling
    // === OBSERVABLE CONTRACT ===============================================
    // Placeholder for observable contract
    // === BOOT ===============================================================
    // Placeholder for boot/start
  </script>
</body>
</html>

That's fine. No console errors: No references to undefined variables: the script just has comments, no code. So should load fine.

